    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/logicSummary> "Prohibits charging a fee in inappropriate circumstances when required";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/premiseText> "(2) This subsection applies if:  (a) any fee (the reasonable fee):  (i) that has been determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person; or  (ii) that can be worked out from a method determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person;  covers either or both of the matters in paragraph (1)(c) of this section; and  (b) the portion of the fee charged as described in that paragraph for those matters exceeds the corresponding portion of the reasonable fee.";
    <https://ns.webcivics.net/cml/conclusionText> "(2) This subsection applies if:  (a) any fee (the reasonable fee):  (i) that has been determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person; or  (ii) that can be worked out from a method determined under subsection 56BV(1) for the person;  covers either or both of the matters in paragraph (1)(c) of this section; and  (b) the portion of the fee charged as described in that paragraph for those matters exceeds the corresponding portion of the reasonable fee.";
